message.content:
Sure! Below is a simple example of an “interactive card” that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML** and **CSS** (no JavaScript).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
body { margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background:#f0f0f0; display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center; height:100vh; }

/* Card container – keeps perspective so rotation looks 3‑D */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    perspective: 800px;          /* gives depth to the 3‑D transform */
}

/* The actual card – front & back sides */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth animation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3‑D space */
    cursor: pointer;
}

/* Front side */
.card .front,
.card .back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%; height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;       /* hide backside while rotated */
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Front styling */
.card .front {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg,#ff9a9e 0%, #fad0c4 100%);
    color:white;
    display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center;
    font-size:1.5rem;
    text-align:center;
}

/* Back styling – rotated 180° so it’s initially hidden */
.card .back {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg,#a18cd1 0%, #fbc2eb 100%);
    transform: rotateY(180deg);        /* start flipped */
    color:white;
    display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center;
    font-size:1.2rem;
    text-align:center;
}

/* Hover effect – flip the whole card */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="front">
            <p>Front Side – Hover me!</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="back">
            <p>Back Side – You see me now.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Sets `perspective`, giving the 3‑D effect. |
| `.card` | Holds both sides; `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps its children in 3‑D space. |
| `.front` / `.back` | Each side is absolutely positioned on top of each other. |
| `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.back` | Starts the back side flipped, so it’s invisible until the card flips. |
| `transition` on `.card` | Smoothly animates the rotation. |

Feel free to replace the gradients, text, or add images inside the `.front` and `.back` divs. Adjust the `width`, `height`, or `perspective` values to fit your design needs. Enjoy creating interactive cards!
